id: pm-history-receipt-cost
title: Measure and bound history receipt costs for indexed append and follow
description: "Complete byte receipts make indexed appends hash the full affected stream before and after each append under the writer lock. Unfiltered follow reads validate every selected stream per iteration. Measure these history-length and stream-count axes, then assess safe caller guidance, polling policy or receipt-state designs while preserving detection of external same-length rewrites. This is separate from pm-29ymfn item-state replay/canonicalization cost."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T13:52:55.362Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T14:25:27.528Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Measure representative history lengths and filtered/unfiltered follow workloads on the release Node major; preserve native same-length tamper and concurrent-receipt controls; record tradeoffs before changing defaults or introducing cheaper receipt state.
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "Local measurements quantify append and follow CPU, IO, wall time and memory before selecting a compatible optimization or cadence policy; complete-history integrity and restore behavior remain protected."
